      "writtenOn": "2022-01-28T18:01:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I believe the memory barrier here is to ensure that all the fpu_state register has cleared before moving on. Without the barrier the compiler could, in theory, reorder some later code such that the fpu_state isn\u0027t cleared yet. \n\nThis actually made me wonder if fpu_state should be defined as a volatile. As it is if CPU_FPU_FPCAR is updated between the previous read and here then it may be overwritten.",
      "parentUuid": "d8db78b4_9a6bdca7",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 114,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 114,
