      "message": "So I think we\u0027re all in sync on `fpu_state[FPU_IDX_REG_FPSCR]` being on the stack and that it\u0027s fine if the compiler does not do a second read when clearing the value on the stack (i.e., `volatile` not necessary). I\u0027m still trying to understand where the memory barrier (`dmb`) comes in. The Linux Kernel requires that barrier instructions have a comment describing the logic of what they are doing and why, and I think that\u0027s a useful idiom: https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/process/submit-checklist.html.\n\nReferences:\n\n* https://community.arm.com/arm-community-blogs/b/architectures-and-processors-blog/posts/memory-access-ordering---an-introduction\n* https://www.kernel.org/doc/Documentation/memory-barriers.txt",
